  args:
    - deactivate
    - "--help"
---
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Deactivate and reboot into the decoy state (unmount + cleanup + reboot)

Usage: nails deactivate [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides binary-relative discovery)

      --no-clear-history
          Skip shell history cleanup

          By default, deactivation removes all 'nails' commands from shell history. Use this flag to preserve history (not recommended for forensic safety).

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace

  -y, --yes
          Proceed without the confirmation prompt

          Deactivation restores the decoy configuration and reboots. Without this flag it prompts on a terminal and refuses to run without one.

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors and the final result

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal, TERM is not `dumb` and NO_COLOR is unset or empty
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour

          [default: auto]

      --ascii
          Use ASCII markers instead of Unicode symbols and box drawing

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on stdout

      --no-log-file
          Do not write the log file on the hidden volume (diagnostics still go to stderr)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
